## 8. Key Takeaways

- Burp Suite extensions add capabilities beyond the platform's built-in tools.
- The BApp Store provides a convenient way to discover and install extensions.
- Request-timing data can help identify behavior worth investigating, but timing differences alone do not prove a vulnerability.
- Jython and JRuby support certain compatible Python- and Ruby-based extensions.
- Extension APIs allow developers to create custom security-testing functionality.
- Runtime compatibility and API support should be verified before installing or developing an extension.

## Conclusion

Burp Suite Extensions make the platform more flexible by allowing testers to add specialized tools, automate workflows, and develop custom functionality. Understanding the Extensions interface, BApp Store, language integration, and extension APIs provides a foundation for using and developing extensions in authorized security-testing environments.
